{"step_index":173,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T14:47:20Z","content":"I hear you loud and clear: **`mtq-mailsrvp-01` joins the DEV zone!**\n\nBefore I make any modifications, here is the technical plan and one critical authentication prerequisite to address, in accordance with our repository rules (*Règle n°1 : expliquer avant de modifier*).\n\n---\n\n### The Prerequisite: Runner Key on `mtq-mailsrvp-01`\n\nRemember the discovery from our reconnaissance:\n* On `mtq-mailsrvp-01`, `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner` currently contains **only** the PROD runner key (`semaphore-runner-prod`).\n* The **DEV runner** (`th2-ansid-run1`) uses the DEV key:\n  ```text\n  ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner\n  ```\n* If we do not append this key, any playbook executed from Semaphore in the DEV inventory will fail with <span style=\"color:red\">**`Permission denied (publickey)`**</span>.\n\nSince `superuser` on `mtq-mailsrvp-01` requires a sudo password, we need to append this line to `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`:\n```bash\necho 'ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner' | sudo tee -a /etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner\n```\n*(Or run `sudo ./bootstrap-spui-runner-manual.sh dev` directly on the server).*\n\n---\n\n### The Implementation Plan (IaC Repo)\n\n1. **Git Branching**:\n   * Create dedicated branch: `feat/onboard-mtq-mailsrvp-dev` from clean `main`.\n2. **Inventory Update** in [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml):\n   * Add host definition under `all.hosts`:\n     ```yaml\n         mtq-mailsrvp-01:\n           ansible_host: 172.30.39.153\n           ansible_port: 30\n     ```\n   * Add dedicated group under `all.children`:\n     ```yaml\n         mail_servers:\n           hosts:\n             mtq-mailsrvp-01:\n     ```\n3. **Verification**:\n   * Test inventory parsing with `ansible-inventory -i inventories/dev/hosts.yml --graph`.\n4. **Git Commit & Push**:\n   * Commit message: `feat(inventory): add mtq-mailsrvp-01 to dev inventory`.\n   * Push branch to GitLab origin to prepare the MR.\n\n---\n\n### Confirmation\nDo you authorize me to branch and apply this change to [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml)? And can you run the one-line `tee -a` command with sudo on `mtq-mailsrvp-01` (or provide the sudo password for `superuser`)?","thinking":"**Listing Target Hosts and Groups**\n\nThe host inventory file reveals the available target hosts and their associated groups. The `databases` group points to a subgroup `mariadb`, which then includes a single host named `trp-wextd-db`. This information clarifies the infrastructure setup.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Requirement**\n\nThe user's request explicitly specifies adding `mtq-mailsrvp-01` to the `DEV` zone. This translates to modifying the `inventories/dev/hosts.yml` file. Further investigation is needed to determine where to place the host within the file. Based on previous instructions, this modification requires a new branch and MR. The branch should be based on a clean `main` and named appropriately.\n\n\n**Addressing SSH Key Authentication**\n\nThe primary challenge is ensuring the DEV runner can authenticate to `mtq-mailsrvp-01`. The current configuration on the target host only allows PROD runner access. Adding the DEV runner's key to the `authorized_keys` file is the solution to avoid SSH authentication errors for DEV tasks.\n\nThe critical next step involves securely adding the DEV key to the authorized keys file. Potential solutions include leveraging user privileges or seeking user input for a `sudo` command. The goal is to safely authorize the DEV runner without compromising the existing PROD setup.\n\n\n"}
